  "elevationPhilosophy": "Monocle rejects drop shadows entirely. Elevation is communicated through surface color shifts (cream → warm white → light yellow → gray) and 1px hairline borders in #d9d9d9. This is a print convention: depth comes from tonal layering on the page, not from cast shadows. Any design agent building for this system should default to flat surfaces with thin rules, never shadowed cards.",
  "imagery": "Photography is editorial and documentarian — tight portrait crops of political figures, architectural exteriors of cities, and product still-lifes. Images are large, full-bleed within their grid cells, and treated without color grading or overlays. Editorial illustrations are flat, geometric, and limited to the brand palette: black line work with #ffc500 yellow fills and occasional #64d5ff blue accents. Illustrations often feature a single character or scene with minimal background. The overall image density is high — this is a publication, not a product page — and imagery carries equal weight to text in the layout.",
